#{[17592186436129 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436122 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436129 #edb/ref 1069 "q-74911" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436129 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436129 #edb/ref 1071 "${lim}_{x\\to (4,-4,-2)}\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{x-y}}{z}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436129 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c11b4e02-4fa9-528c-867b-1ff09ac00c10" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436129 #edb/ref 1074 "The function \n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{x-y}}{z}\n$$\n\nis continuous except when the denominator is zero. However, the point $(4,-4,-2)$ does not cause the  denominator to vanish, so we can calculate the limit by substituting  $(4,-4,-2)$ into the function: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (4,-4,-2)}\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{x-y}}{z} & =\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{4-(-4)}}{(-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{8}}{-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{-2} \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436130 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186436121 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436130 #edb/ref 1069 "q-74959" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436130 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436130 #edb/ref 1071 "${lim}_{x\\to (3,3)}\\frac{\\sqrt{6+y}-x}{6+y-{x}^{2}}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436130 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cdbbe1e3-c4b9-56df-b019-b8be69ef537e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186436130 #edb/ref 1074 "Attempting to evaluate the limit by direct substitution leads to the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ as follows: \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (3,3)}\\frac{\\sqrt{6+y}-x}{6+y-{x}^{2}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{6+3}-3}{6+3-{3}^{2}}=\\frac{0}{0}\n$$\n\nHowever, we can simplify the limit by first multiplying the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (3,3)}\\frac{\\sqrt{6+y}-x}{6+y-{x}^{2}} & ={lim}_{x\\to (3,3)}\\frac{(\\sqrt{6+y}-x)(\\sqrt{6+y}+x)}{(6+y-{x}^{2})(\\sqrt{6+y}+x)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (3,3)}\\frac{(\\sqrt{6+y})^{2}-{x}^{2}}{(6+y-{x}^{2})(\\sqrt{6+y}+x)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (3,3)}\\frac{6+y-{x}^{2}}{(6+y-{x}^{2})(\\sqrt{6+y}+x)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to (3,3)}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6+y}+x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the limit has been simplified, we can evaluate it:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to (3,3)}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6+y}+x} & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6+3}+3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{9}+3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the limit evaluates to $\\frac{1}{6}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
